  "data_abstract": "BNL-RHIC.  Measurements of midrapidity charged particle multiplicity distributions, $dN_{ch}/d\\eta$, and midrapidity transverse-energy distributions, $dE_T/d\\eta$, are presented for a variety of collision systems and energies. Included are distributions for Au+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 200, 130, 62.4, 39, 27,19.6, 14.5, and 7.7 GeV, Cu+Cu collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 200 and 62.4 GeV, Cu+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 200 GeV, U+U collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 193 GeV, d+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 200 GeV, $^3$He+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ 200 GeV, and p+p collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 200 GeV. Centrality dependent distributions at midrapidity are presented in terms of the number of nucleon participants, Npart, and the number of constituent quark participants, $N_{qp}$. For all A+A collisions down to $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 7.7 GeV, it is observed that the midrapidity data are better described by scaling with $N_{qp}$ than scaling with $N_{part}$. Also presented are estimates of the Bjorken energy density, $\\epsilon_{BJ}$, and the ratio of $dET/d\\eta$ to $dNch/d\\eta$, the latter of which is seen to be constant as a function of centrality for all systems.\n",
